    "title": "pandas.Series.sparse.fill_value — pandas 2.3.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Series.sparse.fill_value#\n\n- Series.sparse.fill_value[source]#\n- Elements in data that are fill_value are not stored. For memory savings, this should be the most common value in the array. Examples >>> ser = pd.Series([0, 0, 2, 2, 2], dtype=\"Sparse[int]\") >>> ser.sparse.fill_value 0 >>> spa_dtype = pd.SparseDtype(dtype=np.int32, fill_value=2) >>> ser = pd.Series([0, 0, 2, 2, 2], dtype=spa_dtype) >>> ser.sparse.fill_value 2",
